---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main class="container pb-4">
    <div class="pb-2 mb-2">
      <h1>About me</h1>

      <hr />
    </div>

    <section class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-9 order-2 order-lg-1">
        <p class="lead">
          I am Alejandro Jeronimo Azamar. A usual alias I use is <strong
            >Zama</strong
          >, which is simply a shortened version of my last name.
        </p>
        <p>
          I began studying <strong>Software Engineering</strong> in 2022. Beyond my
          formal education, I completed a semester-long <strong
            >Ruby on Rails Web Developer</strong
          > bootcamp in 2023.
        </p>

        <div class="m-2 my-4 p-3 border">
          <h3>The Learning Process</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            I often pass hours researching things I already know, thinking, <em
              >"Maybe I am doing it wrong?"</em
            > or <em>"I should double-check this..."</em> This curiosity leads me
            to deepen my knowledge, learn new things, and bring out the best in my
            work.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          I started this journey thinking, <em
            >"The career name sounds so cool, complex, and meaningful—I really
            want to study this!"</em
          >
          Coming from a technical accounting background, I barely knew how to turn
          on a machine. My first college assignment was to "Make a game with the PyGame
          framework based on an SDG." So I was like <em>"..."</em>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="col-lg-3 order-1 order-lg-2">
        <div class="m-2 p-3 pt-0 border">
          <p class="text-center my-2">
            <strong>Alejandro Jeronimo Azamar</strong>
          </p>

          <figure>
            <img
              class="img-fluid text-center"
              src="https://github.com/zama15.png"
              alt="GitHub Profile picture of Zama"
            />

            <figcaption class="mt-2 text-muted text-center">
              <small>My GitHub Avatar</small>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <dl class="row mb-0">
            <dt class="col-5">Nationality</dt>
            <dd class="col-7">Mexican</dd>

            <dt class="col-5">Education</dt>
            <dd class="col-7">Universidad de Colima</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4">
      <div class="pb-2 mb-2">
        <h2>Most Recent Projects</h2>

        <hr />
      </div>

      <p class="text-muted mb-4">
        Most of these projects were for my college coursework, but I loved
        working on all of them. I <strong
          >never worked with the same team twice</strong
        >, which made the experience fulfilling and helped me develop the soft
        skills necessary for this field.
      </p>

      <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-3">
        <div class="col">
          <h3>University Repository</h3>
          <p class="small">
            A centralized web/mobile app where students can manage their
            projects and professors can oversee them using an RBAC security
            methodology. I was in charge of the backend, architecture design,
            and database management.
          </p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 small">
            <li>Backend</li>
            <li>Architecture</li>
            <li>DB Management</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="col">
          <h3>Android SPA App</h3>
          <p class="small">
            A mobile app for spas to register their menus and users to schedule
            appointments. Supported real-time calendars and map visualization. I
            acted as a full-stack developer, designing views, backend logic, and
            cloud database management.
          </p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 small">
            <li>Full-Stack</li>
            <li>UI/UX</li>
            <li>Cloud DB</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="col">
          <h3 class="h5 card-title">Custom PHP Framework</h3>
          <p class="small">
            Custom Framework from scratch. Built with it a forum where users
            manage posts and admins oversee content. I led my team through the
            entire process using software management, best practices, and
            methodologies.
          </p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 small">
            <li>PHP</li>
            <li>Leadership</li>
            <li>Best Practices</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="pb-2 mb-2">
        <h2>Skills & Tools</h2>

        <hr />
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
          <h3>Technologies</h3>

          <ul class="list-unstyled mt-3 ms-2">
            <li class="p-2">
              <strong>Linux:</strong> Learned by installing different distros, managing
              servers, and writing scripts. One of my favorite hobbies.
            </li>
            <li class="p-2">
              <strong>Git:</strong> Inspired by highly proficient peers, I pushed
              myself to make version control one of my most robust capabilities.
            </li>
            <li class="p-2">
              <strong>Documentation:</strong> I believe strong, clear documentation
              allows anyone to understand a project without dive too deeply into the
              code.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
          <h3>Languages</h3>

          <dl class="row mt-3 ms-2">
            <dt class="col-4 p-2">Spanish</dt>
            <dd class="col-8 p-2">Native</dd>

            <dt class="col-4 p-2">English</dt>
            <dd class="col-8 p-2">B2 (Cambridge)</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
